  "text": "Làm đềtrực tuyến tại: https://ielts-fighter.com/online-test.html\nWebsite tựhọc IELTS: https://ielts-fighter.com\nWOMAN:\nOK.\nMAN:\nThen they'll probably ask you what sorts of tasks you do for your mother\nduring the day. Things like if she needs help with getting dressed, for example.\nWOMAN:\nRight. I help her with that. And also I help her get into the shower in the\nmorning.\nMAN:\nYes, that sort of thing.\nWOMAN:\nYes, that's becoming a bit of a problem. She used to be very good at it, but not\nanymore.\nBefore you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at\nquestions five to ten. Now listen and answer questions 5 to 10.\nMAN:\nAnd be ready to tell them about anything you find particularly difficult about\ncaring for your mother.\nWOMAN:\nSo, recently I've noticed she's started to have quite bad problems with her\nmemory. If I wasn't there, I think she'd forget to eat, for example. And often\nshe doesn't seem quite sure what day\nMAN:\nYes, tell them about that. And are there any physical difficulties you have\ncaring for her? Lifting her, for example?\nWOMAN:\nYes, she's quite heavy and I'm afraid of hurting my back. I'd be in real trouble if\nthat happened.\n",
